#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# least_squares

#% text
# `least_squares(m, b)` gives the vector `x` that minimizes the norm of `m . x - b`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# For a matrix of less than full rank it gives the solution of least norm, the pseudo-inverse of `m` applied to `b`.

#% item
# A matrix `b` is solved for column by column.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
least_squares([[1, 0], [1, 1], [1, 2]], [1, 2, 2])
#% output
#= [7/6, 1/2]

#% cell
least_squares([[1, 1], [1, 1]], [1, 3])
#% output
#= [1, 1]

#% cell
least_squares([[1., 0.], [1., 1.], [1., 2.]], [1., 2., 2.])
#% output
#= [1.1666666666666663, 0.5]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `pseudo_inverse`, `fit`
